Project Testing Phase

The Project Testing Phase is the stage where the developed project is checked for errors, bugs, performance, and correctness before it is released.

Main Points:

Check Functionality – Verify that every feature works correctly.
Find Bugs – Identify errors and problems in the system.
Test User Interface – Check buttons, pages, forms, and navigation.
Test Performance – Make sure the system works smoothly and responds quickly.
Fix and Retest – Correct the problems and test again to ensure they are solved.
